The canonical license identifier and URL are recorded in `LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-4.0.txt`. Complete copies of the upstream license are included as `LICENSE` inside every packaged ARSU Skill directory.

The MIT grant does not remove or override the noncommercial restriction on ARSU-derived material. Commercial distribution or use of the combined package may require separate permission from the relevant rights holder. This file documents the project's engineering interpretation and is not legal advice.

## Apache-2.0 material

Generated FinRobot-derived Skills under `skills/plugins/vendors/finrobot/**`
and independently reimplemented HistAgent-derived Skills under
`skills/plugins/vendors/histagent/**` are distributed under Apache License 2.0
after source, origin, license, and derivation review. Each Skill contains its
complete `LICENSE`, attribution `NOTICE`, source revision, and derivation
manifest. A reference copy of the license is available at
`LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt`.

The Apache-2.0 grant applies only to the reviewed FinRobot- and HistAgent-derived material
identified by those files and does not change the licenses of ARSU-derived,
ResearchSpec-authored, or other vendor material.
